        "statement": "Reporting defects, counterexamples or already-required behaviour alone is not authorship. Adopted wording, design or policy, including particular repair directions, is authorship of that contribution; calling it a finding does not restore independence. Finding a defect grants no review authority. Reading the same governing sources is allowed, but a fresh context grants neither independence nor authority; self-review remains construction output. Received contributions retain their author's identity wherever carried, and that author's reading is not independent acceptance. Independence across actor families must be declared; absent a stated policy, two activations of one model family are not independent for semantic judgment.",
